From: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: enable the DRAM half of the PPE table

airoha_ppe_hw_init() programs REG_PPE_TB_HASH_CFG with a mask that already
names PPE_DRAM_TABLE_EN_MASK, but the value side only sets the SRAM enable
and SRAM hash1 bits.  The read-modify-write therefore clears the DRAM
table enable, and the same is true for PPE_DRAM_HASH1_EN_MASK, which is
missing from the mask and so is never touched at all.

The PPE entry count still advertises both halves --
airoha_ppe_get_num_stats_entries() adds the DRAM share from
PPE_DRAM_TB_NUM_ENTRY_MASK -- so the hash folds across 16384 DRAM entries
that are guaranteed to miss, while airoha_ppe_foe_commit_entry() only
handshakes the SRAM half (`if (hash < sram_num_entries)`).  Every flow
that lands in the DRAM half is committed as if it were an SRAM entry, the
PPE never sees it, and the traffic quietly falls back to the CPU path.

Enable the DRAM table and its hash1 engine so the folded range the driver
advertises is the range the hardware actually searches.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <openwrt@example.org>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -214,12 +214,15 @@
 			      PPE_SRAM_TABLE_EN_MASK |
 			      PPE_SRAM_HASH1_EN_MASK |
 			      PPE_DRAM_TABLE_EN_MASK |
+			      PPE_DRAM_HASH1_EN_MASK |
 			      PPE_SRAM_HASH0_MODE_MASK |
 			      PPE_SRAM_HASH1_MODE_MASK |
 			      PPE_DRAM_HASH0_MODE_MASK |
 			      PPE_DRAM_HASH1_MODE_MASK,
 			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_SRAM_TABLE_EN_MASK, 1) |
 			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_SRAM_HASH1_EN_MASK, 1) |
+			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_DRAM_TABLE_EN_MASK, 1) |
+			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_DRAM_HASH1_EN_MASK, 1) |
 			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_SRAM_HASH1_MODE_MASK, 1) |
 			      FIELD_PREP(PPE_DRAM_HASH1_MODE_MASK, 3));
 
